sumer-absence/staleness arm of the lifecycle unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8d636bc957855e7f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 1 (serving_gauge / hold_background_work) and 2 (spawn_context_daemon takes the hold)","norm_id":"n6d38fcc830afe7c3","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CLI `rebar verify-completion` (or a library facade call) spawns a context daemon through spawn_context_daemon with no serving gauge bound in the context-local; if hold()/hold_background_work() assumes a bound gauge it either raises or silently no-ops, and the plan never says which."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 1, specify that hold_background_work() returns an idempotent no-op release when context-local serving_gauge is unset, and that spawn_context_daemon's CLI/library callers rely on that behavior.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '`rebar store fsck` reports `UNCERTIFIED_CLOSE` (report-only, `counted: false`) f' cites operational evidence (live_run, store_op) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the explicit upper bound wait_for_idle honors (reuse DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS or a named cap) and confirm the stdio path — which has no preceding drain_then_exit — is covered, so a hung spawn_context_daemon daemon cannot block run_mcp from returning without an external supervisor.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3433,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Add wait_for_idle(gauge), which run_mcp runs in a finally before returning ... There is no new deadline: the tracked work is already bounded by its own caps (the gate hard cap), and Docker's stop --time stays the outer bound.'","run_mcp stdio branch (src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py:154-158) has no SIGTERM drain_then_exit — the HTTP grace path is HTTP-only, so wait_for_idle would be the sole wait for stdio","spawn_context_daemon is also used by run_workflow (src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:112), whose _bg runs workflow steps, not a gate bounded by the gate hard cap"],"finding":"wait_for_idle is specified with no deadline and is the ONLY wait on the stdio path (no drain_then_exit precedes it there); the plan's bound for it is the asserted 'gate hard cap' + 'Docker stop --time', but run_workflow daemons spawned through spawn_context_daemon execute arbitrary workflow steps (not only the hard-capped gate) and a stdio invocation may have no Docker supervisor, so a hung daemon could block run_mcp from returning indefinitely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f354d42084bc2eff5","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 (src/rebar/_mcp_serving.py: wait_for_idle); 'There is no new deadline' sentence","norm_id":"ne0bde8beaedb2fc6","priority":0.2567,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A workflow daemon hangs or runs long under stdio transport with no container stop-timer; run_mcp's finally blocks on wait_for_idle with no bound","A gate daemon exceeds expectations and the only backstop (Docker stop --time) is absent in a non-container run"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give wait_for_idle the same bounded, injectable-clock signature as drain_then_exit (grace_seconds defaulting to DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS) and note it applies on both transports, so a stuck daemon degrades to a bounded wait then cleanup rather than an unbounded block.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod